## Blind-spot audit and second collection

First pass could not distinguish direct PMP22 cis regulation from a broad repair/differentiation shift. Followed EGR2 upstream to NRG/ERBB/YY1 regulation of Egr2-AS and EZH2/WDR5 chromatin mechanisms, using PMC11592338 primary source and GEO context. Retained the RNA contradiction. Expanded panel to Mtor, AP-1, lipid and protein-quality-control genes; no inference of pathway activity from transcript alone.

Selected three additional processed narrowPeak gzip files using bio fetch (GFP1 already local); total newly acquired measurement bytes 3,482,280. Acquired revisions: asset_5af4bd06c28c3f88d7b4cde500f161bd, asset_dbbd6e785b9997688f2be7d6ace37d76, asset_b59cf55f51237ff92b69d16a70bdb77d. Inspected each through bio. analyze_atac.py reads immutable gzip bytes, not author code. Reference asset_c3bc524f6b0d57c01d1709dec24cf801 is rn6 by parent UCSC URL; used strand-aware -1500/+500 windows, no rn5/rn6 mixing. Egr2 and Jun have called peaks in all libraries. The single selected RefSeq Pmp22 promoter has no called overlap; that is selected-list absence, not a measured zero or proof of no accessibility. Promoter completeness and source-reference version unresolved. This follow-up did not establish a direct cis mechanism.

Broadened interpretation to miR-29, TEAD/YAP/TAZ and protein turnover, and distinguished PMP22-to-ABCA1 consequence from unproven feedback. No new causal biological discovery claimed; upstream antisense control is an established published mechanism newly incorporated in this question.

